    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S009",
      "patient_response": "Nice to meet you, Dr. Smith. Well, what brings me in is... I just keep forgetting things I really shouldn’t. Important stuff, you know? Like my heart follow-up appointments, and then I forget to call the clinic back to reschedule. \n\nThough, to be fair, calling that clinic is a full-time job. They have that new automated system where you press one for this, two for that, and you just sit on hold listening to that awful saxophone music. My buddy Lou used to work for the phone company back in the seventies, and he says those systems are actually designed to make you hang up. Makes sense to me. \n\nBut anyway, it's not just the doctors. I'll go to do a repair job—I do a little handyman work here and there since I stopped working—and I'll show up without the right tools. I'll get all the way over there and realize the specific wrench I need is sitting right on my kitchen counter next to the toaster. We just got a new toaster, actually. One of those shiny silver ones with four slots. Burns the bagels every time if you aren't watching it like a hawk. \n\nBut yeah... what were we talking about? Oh, right, just forgetting stuff like that all the time. It's getting really frustrating.",
