    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Are these difficulties with focus and organization causing problems in more than one area of your life, such as at home, in your relationships, or in your social life?",
      "targeted_symptom": "functional_impairment",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, it really is causing trouble all over. Like I was saying before about the doctors... my doctor’s office has had to actually chase me down about those missed heart follow-ups. The nurse who usually calls me, Brenda, she's a real sweetheart. She makes this incredible pecan pie for the charity bake sale every November. You know, the secret to a really good pecan pie is using dark corn syrup, none of that light stuff. My wife used to use the light syrup and it just never set right, always came out runny and soaked right through the crust. But Brenda, she knows exactly what she's doing. \n\nAnyway, Brenda's always having to call me because I just don't show up. And then, well, down at the senior center... I help out with this repair group there. We fix up chairs and little things for folks. But it’s gotten to where they just can’t count on me the way they used to. I'll completely forget it's my day to be there, or I'll show up and start taking apart the breakroom coffee machine instead of doing what I'm supposed to. That coffee machine is a total piece of junk, by the way. It's one of those old percolators that makes the coffee taste like burnt pennies. You ever had coffee like that? It just coats your tongue and ruins your whole morning. But yeah, I guess it's definitely messing things up for me with the group and the doctors.",
