    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you still find it difficult to sit still for long periods, or do you feel a need to be constantly moving?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Oh, absolutely. I just can't sit still. Especially lately. Since I've had to slow down on my walks and my little repair projects, sitting around just makes me feel like I've got a motor running inside me and nowhere good to put all that energy. \n\nIt reminds me of this old Ford pickup I used to have in my twenties. Beautiful truck, cherry red, but the idle was always set too high. You'd be sitting at a red light and the whole cab would just vibrate, like it was begging to take off. I tried adjusting the carburetor myself a dozen times, but I could never get it quite right. My neighbor, Mr. Henderson, he told me it was the timing belt, but what did he know? He drove a station wagon with wood paneling on the side. You don't see those anymore, do you? The wood paneling, I mean. It always peeled off after a few years anyway, looked terrible. \n\nBut yeah... sitting still is just awful for me. I always feel like I need to be doing something with my hands or getting up to check on something.",
